1
00:00:01,634 --> 00:00:02,569
TOUTEI HOSPITAL

2
00:00:02,635 --> 00:00:04,104
We have an announcement to make.

3
00:00:04,604 --> 00:00:06,973
In this month's medical journal ranking,

4
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:10,377
Toutei Hospital finally
entered the top ten.

5
00:00:11,544 --> 00:00:13,446
- That's amazing.
- Congratulations.

6
00:00:15,115 --> 00:00:16,416
All right. All right.

7
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:18,985
It's too early to be that happy.

8
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:22,722
Meanwhile, Keirin Hospital
ranked as No.1...

9
00:00:22,856 --> 00:00:24,591
received a three-page
feature spread.

10
00:00:24,991 --> 00:00:27,427
An interview with Director Samejima
is also published.

11
00:00:27,794 --> 00:00:32,465
This man, Director Samejima,

12
00:00:32,565 --> 00:00:36,069
is open to receive filthy bribes.

13
00:00:37,337 --> 00:00:41,441
In order to lift his surgery success rate,
he avoids dangerous procedures.

14
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:47,647
He is a disgrace to
hospital directors everywhere.

15
00:00:48,014 --> 00:00:50,583
Yes sir.
He is truly a terrible man.

16
00:00:51,017 --> 00:00:52,018
Who are you to talk?

17
00:00:53,319 --> 00:00:56,056
- Substitute-Chief Surgeon Kaji.
- Yes?

18
00:00:56,122 --> 00:00:57,424
- Did you say something?
- No.

19
00:00:58,558 --> 00:01:00,393
Show me results!

20
00:01:00,994 --> 00:01:02,796
- Yes sir.
- Defeat Keirin!

21
00:01:03,596 --> 00:01:04,931
Defeat Keirin.

22
00:01:04,998 --> 00:01:06,032
Defeat Keirin!

23
00:01:06,499 --> 00:01:07,734
Defeat Keirin!

24
00:01:07,867 --> 00:01:09,803
You're far too quiet!

25
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:11,971
- Excuse me!
- Yes?

26
00:01:15,375 --> 00:01:17,143
It's 5 p.m., so I'm going home.

27
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:18,812
Hold on right there.

28
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:20,880
Daimon! You dumb!

29
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:23,450
- You dumb!
- Stop there, you dumb!

30
00:01:23,583 --> 00:01:26,286
THE 55TH PARTY FOR KEIRIN AND
TOUTEI WOMEN'S ASSOCATION

31
00:01:29,422 --> 00:01:32,759
I had the pleasure of reading
the interview with your husband.

32
00:01:33,159 --> 00:01:35,862
We are no match to Keirin.

33
00:01:36,963 --> 00:01:38,364
What are you talking about?

34
00:01:38,965 --> 00:01:44,003
Toutei has recently shown...
a great deal of improvement.

35
00:01:45,071 --> 00:01:46,706
Do you remember what place...

36
00:01:47,941 --> 00:01:49,409
Toutei was in until recently?

37
00:01:49,709 --> 00:01:51,211
It was ranked as 38th.

38
00:01:52,178 --> 00:01:56,583
It's really hard to believe
that they were ranked as 38th.

39
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,420
Now we are in the 9th place.

40
00:02:00,487 --> 00:02:04,057
Oh, my. It has become a single digit.

41
00:02:05,725 --> 00:02:07,026
That is splendid.

42
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:08,394
How wonderful.

43
00:02:08,461 --> 00:02:10,430
Thank you very much.

44
00:02:19,372 --> 00:02:20,240
What is going on?

45
00:02:20,373 --> 00:02:21,508
What a bad vibe!

46
00:02:21,908 --> 00:02:23,943
Michiko, over here.

47
00:02:24,077 --> 00:02:25,745
Mr. Akira!

48
00:02:25,945 --> 00:02:29,082
I'm going to dig right in!
Thank you.

49
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,951
Don't be greedy.

50
00:02:32,018 --> 00:02:35,388
I barely got their permission
to attend this event...

51
00:02:35,455 --> 00:02:37,157
after almost begging them.

52
00:02:37,223 --> 00:02:40,326
Those people don't seem
to be socialising at all.

53
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,663
Toutei and Keirin
have been rivals for many years,

54
00:02:43,830 --> 00:02:47,066
but Keirin obviously
has a higher ranking now.

55
00:02:47,467 --> 00:02:51,437
The hospital ranking reflects
the women's association ranking.

56
00:02:51,504 --> 00:02:53,006
Just take a look at that.

57
00:02:53,106 --> 00:02:57,010
Director Hiruma's wife is going to
burst a blood vessel any second.

58
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:01,181
How nostalgic! It looks like
kids staring at each other.

59
00:03:01,514 --> 00:03:05,585
Let's compete at the coming
social dance contest.

60
00:03:05,785 --> 00:03:08,021
This will be our year.

61
00:03:08,154 --> 00:03:09,923
I see.

62
00:03:10,323 --> 00:03:13,893
You surely must win at least
something like dancing.

63
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:15,662
- That's right.
- That's right.

64
00:03:15,828 --> 00:03:17,463
- Dancing?
- Yes.

65
00:03:17,931 --> 00:03:21,434
The two women's associations hold...

66
00:03:21,568 --> 00:03:23,236
a social dance contest every year.

67
00:03:25,004 --> 00:03:28,007
Keirin has won every contest.

68
00:03:28,341 --> 00:03:33,746
By the way, I'm here to make connections
with those people from Keirin.

69
00:03:33,813 --> 00:03:34,647
Again?

70
00:03:35,782 --> 00:03:36,649
Bye bye.

71
00:03:37,250 --> 00:03:38,818
Here you are.

72
00:03:40,286 --> 00:03:41,387
It's a melon.

73
00:03:41,521 --> 00:03:42,922
Excuse me.

74
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:45,858
I am from Kanbara
excellent physician referral centre.

75
00:03:45,925 --> 00:03:48,228
Here is a melon
for our good relationship.

76
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,098
Excellent physician referral centre?

77
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:55,902
We have a large number
of skilled freelance physicians.

78
00:03:56,369 --> 00:03:59,272
Michiko. Michiko.
Introduce yourself.

79
00:03:59,806 --> 00:04:00,907
- Hurry up.
- What?

80
00:04:01,007 --> 00:04:01,908
Hurry up.

81
00:04:05,044 --> 00:04:06,813
I'm Surgeon Michiko Daimon.

82
00:04:07,313 --> 00:04:10,450
Daimon, who never fails no matter
what the surgery may be,

83
00:04:10,516 --> 00:04:11,918
is our most recommended doctor.

84
00:04:12,318 --> 00:04:15,421
She is currently under contract
at Toutei University Hospital.

85
00:04:16,189 --> 00:04:17,523
Can you perform any kind of surgeries?

86
00:04:22,362 --> 00:04:27,433
Well then, with the social dance
contest coming up next month,

87
00:04:27,834 --> 00:04:29,068
We'll now enjoy...

88
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:32,005
the brief dance demonstration
of both associations.

89
00:04:35,341 --> 00:04:37,543
- Watch them.
- They're going to dance?

90
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:02,001
Emi is as amazing as I expected.

91
00:05:02,468 --> 00:05:05,271
We will surely be the winner
again this year.

92
00:05:11,644 --> 00:05:14,113
She is very good.

93
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:41,808
- Mr. Akira, call an ambulance.
- Got it.

94
00:05:44,310 --> 00:05:45,144
Ms. Emi.

95
00:05:46,446 --> 00:05:48,147
Michiko Daimon.

96
00:05:48,448 --> 00:05:51,718
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

97
00:05:53,052 --> 00:05:54,320
<i>In 2016,</i>

98
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:57,290
<i>the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

99
00:05:58,057 --> 00:06:00,026
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

100
00:06:00,293 --> 00:06:02,161
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

101
00:06:03,296 --> 00:06:05,031
<i>Famous university hospitals use...</i>

102
00:06:05,498 --> 00:06:07,900
<i>their brand power</i>
<i>to push into the world.</i>

103
00:06:08,101 --> 00:06:10,803
<i>On the other hand,</i>
<i>highly skilled surgeons...</i>

104
00:06:11,304 --> 00:06:14,374
<i>in pursuit of a higher salary</i>
<i>were relocating to foreign countries.</i>

105
00:06:15,441 --> 00:06:18,411
<i>The world of surgery</i>
<i>has finally emerged...</i>

106
00:06:18,711 --> 00:06:22,181
<i>into the global world</i>
<i>of survival of the fittest.</i>

107
00:06:23,182 --> 00:06:24,050
<i>In the midst of it,</i>

108
00:06:24,384 --> 00:06:27,620
<i>a new breed of doctor has emerged.</i>
<i>Freelance doctors,</i>

109
00:06:27,687 --> 00:06:28,955
Her right atrium is in bad shape.

110
00:06:29,021 --> 00:06:30,490
Get an emergency CT and x-ray done.

111
00:06:30,556 --> 00:06:31,557
Got it.

112
00:06:31,758 --> 00:06:34,827
in other words, lone doctors.

113
00:06:35,828 --> 00:06:37,764
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

114
00:06:38,364 --> 00:06:41,033
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

115
00:06:41,567 --> 00:06:43,136
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

116
00:06:43,603 --> 00:06:46,506
<i>Her solo weapons are her license...</i>

117
00:06:47,106 --> 00:06:48,708
<i>and the skills that she has earned.</i>

118
00:06:49,308 --> 00:06:51,444
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

119
00:06:52,078 --> 00:06:53,012
<i>Also known as</i>

120
00:06:53,646 --> 00:06:55,081
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

121
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,440
It says 120 years.

122
00:07:20,606 --> 00:07:23,543
- Wow, I will live that long?
- You will.

123
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:25,578
- Which one indicates...
- Excuse me.

124
00:07:26,612 --> 00:07:28,114
Director!

125
00:07:28,181 --> 00:07:29,715
- Director!
- What is it? What?

126
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,217
- Your...
- What?

127
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:33,085
- Your...
- I said what is it!

128
00:07:33,152 --> 00:07:34,687
She's coming.

129
00:07:34,754 --> 00:07:35,922
I'm coming in.

130
00:07:38,658 --> 00:07:39,592
Your wife is here.

131
00:07:39,992 --> 00:07:40,993
Yes, that's right.

132
00:07:41,794 --> 00:07:44,297
- My contact lens.
- Oh, what brings you here so suddenly?

133
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:45,998
I need to talk to you.

134
00:07:46,365 --> 00:07:47,800
- Talk?
- I need a moment of your time.

135
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:51,137
- Oh, here it is.
- Oh, you found it?

136
00:07:51,604 --> 00:07:54,774
A patient from the Keirin women's
association has come here?

137
00:07:54,841 --> 00:07:57,109
Michiko Daimon brought her here.

138
00:07:57,610 --> 00:07:59,412
Michiko Daimon did? Oh my.

139
00:07:59,979 --> 00:08:04,283
She's such a senseless woman.
She's nothing but a part-timer.

140
00:08:04,617 --> 00:08:06,552
She said it's because
this hospital was closer.

141
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:08,721
Still, she can't do that.

142
00:08:08,788 --> 00:08:10,656
Send her back to Keirin immediately.

143
00:08:10,723 --> 00:08:11,958
Yes, let's do so.

144
00:08:12,124 --> 00:08:15,895
Kikawada, transfer the patient to Keirin.

145
00:08:16,128 --> 00:08:16,963
Yes sir.

146
00:08:19,999 --> 00:08:21,734
I heard about what happened.

147
00:08:22,435 --> 00:08:25,104
Do you think we can send away a patient

148
00:08:25,171 --> 00:08:26,973
who was just brought here by an ambulance?

149
00:08:27,106 --> 00:08:30,076
Do you think you can properly
manage the hospital...

150
00:08:31,210 --> 00:08:32,612
if you just do what
your novice wife tells you to?

151
00:08:33,546 --> 00:08:35,314
You must be Deputy Director Kubo.

152
00:08:36,883 --> 00:08:39,185
I've heard all about you
from my husband.

153
00:08:39,385 --> 00:08:41,821
I'd love to hear exactly what he told you.

154
00:08:41,954 --> 00:08:44,524
Why don't you talk about that later?

155
00:08:44,590 --> 00:08:45,458
In any case,

156
00:08:46,659 --> 00:08:50,530
I can never... tolerate this hospital...

157
00:08:50,596 --> 00:08:52,999
accepting a patient from Keirin.

158
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:58,538
How ridiculous.
Now I see why you're his wife.

159
00:08:59,005 --> 00:09:00,106
What was that?

160
00:09:00,773 --> 00:09:02,575
Ex-director Kubo's baby sister!

161
00:09:02,642 --> 00:09:05,545
Hana! Hana, calm down.

162
00:09:05,611 --> 00:09:06,579
Enough already!

163
00:09:06,913 --> 00:09:09,849
As the president of the women's
association I will send her away.

164
00:09:10,783 --> 00:09:13,953
- Excuse me.
- Thank you for coming.

165
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:21,694
Your wife is such a beautiful lady.

166
00:09:26,332 --> 00:09:29,669
Kikawada, why are you still here?

167
00:09:29,735 --> 00:09:31,203
I saw something terrifying.

168
00:09:34,206 --> 00:09:35,141
How do you feel?

169
00:09:35,808 --> 00:09:37,109
Much better.

170
00:09:37,643 --> 00:09:39,512
Thank you very much for yesterday.

171
00:09:40,379 --> 00:09:43,349
We have found a blockage
in your pulmonary artery.

172
00:09:43,816 --> 00:09:45,484
Has this ever
happened to you before?

173
00:09:46,018 --> 00:09:46,852
No.

174
00:09:47,587 --> 00:09:51,057
Can you perform the surgery?

175
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:53,559
So you know you need
to get a surgery.

176
00:09:54,360 --> 00:09:56,095
I am a doctor's wife after all.

177
00:09:57,863 --> 00:10:00,066
We must still go through a
more detailed examination,

178
00:10:00,132 --> 00:10:02,068
but if you need the surgery,
I'll be performing.

179
00:10:03,302 --> 00:10:05,338
That's not your decision to make!

180
00:10:06,539 --> 00:10:07,940
The leader of the punks!

181
00:10:08,074 --> 00:10:12,178
Ms. Kujyo, we will be returning
you to Keirin hospital.

182
00:10:12,678 --> 00:10:13,512
Why?

183
00:10:13,913 --> 00:10:17,883
It's simple. She is a member
of the Keirin women's association.

184
00:10:18,551 --> 00:10:20,353
Wouldn't it be better for you, too?

185
00:10:25,024 --> 00:10:26,559
Excuse me.

186
00:10:26,692 --> 00:10:28,995
- Ms. Emi.
- Ms. Emi.

187
00:10:29,795 --> 00:10:32,999
Ms. Emi, how are you feeling?

188
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:38,971
Everyone from Keirin, thank you so much
for coming here to pick her up.

189
00:10:40,773 --> 00:10:41,774
Excuse me?

190
00:10:44,176 --> 00:10:47,880
We're here just to see
how she's doing here.

191
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:50,116
- Isn't that right?
- Of course.

192
00:10:50,282 --> 00:10:55,821
We'd like you to treat
Ms. Emi here.

193
00:10:56,789 --> 00:10:59,492
We're relieved as long as she's here.

194
00:10:59,558 --> 00:11:02,628
- She's right.
- Isn't that right, Emi?

195
00:11:04,363 --> 00:11:05,197
Yes.

196
00:11:07,033 --> 00:11:08,167
Dr. Daimon.

197
00:11:10,636 --> 00:11:12,038
Please take care of me.

198
00:11:13,739 --> 00:11:16,342
Okay.

199
00:11:16,409 --> 00:11:19,045
Why did you say okay?

200
00:11:19,278 --> 00:11:22,214
A part-timer like you can't just
accept a patient like that!

201
00:11:22,281 --> 00:11:25,484
Why not?
She wants us to treat her here.

202
00:11:25,618 --> 00:11:28,587
You're just a part-timer.
Think before you talk!

203
00:11:29,088 --> 00:11:32,858
However, I'm not so sure if other women

204
00:11:33,392 --> 00:11:35,094
from the Keirin association

205
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:37,363
are okay with this.

206
00:11:37,496 --> 00:11:41,233
They're mocking us.
They see us as their sub-organisation.

207
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:44,437
You're going to leave it like this?
Aren't you mortified?

208
00:11:44,503 --> 00:11:45,705
Can I go home?

209
00:11:45,771 --> 00:11:47,406
- Wait!
- Actually,

210
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:51,911
I believe if we are able to treat
a Keirin professor's wife here,

211
00:11:52,311 --> 00:11:54,180
it will appeal to the public.

212
00:11:54,647 --> 00:11:56,248
I suppose that is so.

213
00:11:56,882 --> 00:11:57,883
Then,

214
00:11:57,950 --> 00:12:03,589
shall we accept the
pulmonary embolism patient?

215
00:12:04,490 --> 00:12:08,661
If we do so, they owe us one.

216
00:12:09,628 --> 00:12:10,996
I don't think it's a bad idea.

217
00:12:11,497 --> 00:12:12,331
What?

218
00:12:13,999 --> 00:12:17,670
Director. Considering
the sensitive nature of this case,

219
00:12:17,770 --> 00:12:20,506
I think it would be better not
to have a part-timer operate.

220
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:23,409
Why? She asked me to do it!

221
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:26,746
I'm also convinced
we need to change her doctor.

222
00:12:26,812 --> 00:12:28,881
- I agree.
- Of course.

223
00:12:29,381 --> 00:12:33,085
Who believes that the attending
physician should be changed?

224
00:12:33,219 --> 00:12:34,053
- Yes.
- Yes.

225
00:12:34,353 --> 00:12:39,024
Decision to change a doctor
is adopted by majority.

226
00:12:39,325 --> 00:12:41,293
- Thank you, Daimon.
- Goodbye.

227
00:12:41,894 --> 00:12:44,463
Even so, it is a mystery.

228
00:12:45,765 --> 00:12:46,599
Yes.

229
00:12:46,665 --> 00:12:48,134
Why would a member of the Keirin

230
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:50,202
association want to stay here?

231
00:12:51,704 --> 00:12:53,873
What are you doing here, Daimon?

232
00:12:53,939 --> 00:12:55,775
I want to do the surgery.

233
00:12:55,841 --> 00:12:57,743
There she goes again,
trying to steal operations.

234
00:12:57,810 --> 00:12:59,445
- Right, Chief Surgeon Kaji?
- Yes.

235
00:13:00,079 --> 00:13:02,548
This could be an advantage
for us to get upper hand...

236
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,784
on Keirin University Hospital.

237
00:13:04,850 --> 00:13:07,286
That is why they counted
a part-timer like you out.

238
00:13:07,353 --> 00:13:09,288
There's no operation
that's not important.

239
00:13:09,355 --> 00:13:11,023
There's nothing you can do about it.

240
00:13:11,223 --> 00:13:12,758
- Oh.
- What is it?

241
00:13:13,259 --> 00:13:15,327
It's lunch time!

242
00:13:16,529 --> 00:13:18,998
Don't forget that
you're just a part-timer.

243
00:13:19,865 --> 00:13:22,034
That is correct, Substitute
Chief Surgeon Kaji.

244
00:13:22,101 --> 00:13:23,068
Yes.

245
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:26,071
Dr. Daimon.

246
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:30,075
Are you Dr. Daimon?

247
00:13:30,709 --> 00:13:33,279
Thank you very much for
taking care of my wife yesterday.

248
00:13:34,413 --> 00:13:38,184
I am a surgeon at Keirin hospital.

249
00:13:38,417 --> 00:13:39,451
Please call me Kujyo.

250
00:13:40,219 --> 00:13:42,555
Please continue
to look after my wife.

251
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:45,825
Your husband won't operate?

252
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:46,992
Sorry?

253
00:13:47,459 --> 00:13:48,961
Well, you're a surgeon, right?

254
00:13:50,029 --> 00:13:51,297
Yes, but...

255
00:13:51,730 --> 00:13:53,465
If I make him do my surgery,

256
00:13:53,532 --> 00:13:55,868
I wouldn't know what kind of
mistake he may make.

257
00:13:56,702 --> 00:13:58,070
I'd rather just die.

258
00:13:59,471 --> 00:14:00,573
So you're bad at operating.

259
00:14:02,408 --> 00:14:07,179
They call him a loser surgeon
at Keirin Hospital.

260
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:08,981
His promotion takes forever,

261
00:14:09,348 --> 00:14:12,418
so my influence in the association
also shrank.

262
00:14:12,651 --> 00:14:16,522
I feel ashamed
making you feel that way.

263
00:14:16,889 --> 00:14:19,491
Hurry up and get back to work.

264
00:14:20,326 --> 00:14:21,160
Okay.

265
00:14:21,660 --> 00:14:23,028
- Excuse us.
- Goodbye.

266
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,432
- It's fine.
- Okay.

267
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:43,048
It is a pulmonary embolism. Right?

268
00:14:44,950 --> 00:14:49,021
Dr. Daimon, I have heard all about
how excellent doctor you are.

269
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:53,158
I sincerely ask you
to take care of my wife.

270
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:25,457
The tumour marker on the blood test
is the within normal range.

271
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:47,813
As the chief
of the internal medicine,

272
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:50,349
I believe that long term treatment

273
00:15:50,416 --> 00:15:52,851
through medicine would be effective.

274
00:15:52,918 --> 00:15:54,486
I see.

275
00:15:54,954 --> 00:15:57,389
Well, examine her with caution.

276
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:02,795
For us,
she is a very important hostage.

277
00:16:02,928 --> 00:16:05,764
I mean, as a patient here.

278
00:16:05,898 --> 00:16:06,732
Yes sir.

279
00:16:07,399 --> 00:16:09,868
We're reaching out our hands...

280
00:16:10,336 --> 00:16:14,306
to help our rival... on a sinking ship.

281
00:16:14,707 --> 00:16:16,342
- Kikawada.
- Yes?

282
00:16:16,942 --> 00:16:19,078
Isn't that an impressive story?

283
00:16:19,645 --> 00:16:21,880
I've never heard of
such an impressive story.

284
00:16:25,918 --> 00:16:26,785
Director.

285
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:30,689
Keirin's Director Samejima
sent you something.

286
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:32,591
From Keirin?

287
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:36,829
There are 12 pastries here.

288
00:16:37,296 --> 00:16:40,532
Let's take one out.

289
00:16:41,133 --> 00:16:42,601
Let's take another out.

290
00:16:49,608 --> 00:16:50,509
Dr. Daimon.

291
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:53,579
I would like to do one more test.

292
00:17:15,434 --> 00:17:20,139
Emi Kujyo, 46 years old.
Her diagnosis is a pulmonary embolism.

293
00:17:21,607 --> 00:17:23,108
We have found an embolism...

294
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:25,377
on the right pulmonary artery.

295
00:17:26,378 --> 00:17:29,915
We believe that surgery
is the best treatment option.

296
00:17:29,982 --> 00:17:32,684
A pulmonary endarterectomy.

297
00:17:33,285 --> 00:17:35,220
It is not a particularly
difficult surgery.

298
00:17:35,421 --> 00:17:36,255
Right.

299
00:17:36,321 --> 00:17:37,389
You can't be confident.

300
00:17:37,923 --> 00:17:40,059
Every surgery involves risks.

301
00:17:41,527 --> 00:17:45,397
I think that anticoagulation and
thrombolytic therapies are better.

302
00:17:45,464 --> 00:17:46,298
In other words,

303
00:17:46,665 --> 00:17:47,900
internal medicine will work.

304
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:49,034
Yes sir.

305
00:17:49,101 --> 00:17:50,169
At this rate,

306
00:17:50,669 --> 00:17:52,304
there is the risk of sudden death

307
00:17:52,805 --> 00:17:54,173
by artery blockage.

308
00:17:55,007 --> 00:17:56,508
Early stage surgery is required.

309
00:17:56,909 --> 00:17:57,743
Yes sir.

310
00:17:57,976 --> 00:18:00,746
As the chief of internal medicine,
it is my decision.

311
00:18:00,813 --> 00:18:02,014
Yes sir.

312
00:18:03,048 --> 00:18:05,250
While Dr. Saionji is away,

313
00:18:06,885 --> 00:18:07,953
I am...

314
00:18:09,121 --> 00:18:13,058
the surgical chief.

315
00:18:13,826 --> 00:18:14,827
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

316
00:18:24,069 --> 00:18:26,605
Dr. Daimon,
we didn't ask you to come today.

317
00:18:31,076 --> 00:18:32,945
I'll take this surgery on.

318
00:18:33,979 --> 00:18:37,883
We won't need any surgery. Much less,
you would never be the one to do so.

319
00:18:37,950 --> 00:18:40,219
Daimon, why are you doing this
at the last minute?

320
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:41,753
You just want to do every operation.
Stop it already!

321
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:44,423
None of you are able to manage this.

322
00:18:44,556 --> 00:18:45,724
- What?
- Huh?

323
00:18:52,331 --> 00:18:53,799
A PET-CT.

324
00:18:56,001 --> 00:18:56,835
This is...

325
00:18:57,369 --> 00:18:58,237
No way.

326
00:18:58,971 --> 00:19:01,573
- What is it?
- A pulmonary sarcoma.

327
00:19:02,808 --> 00:19:04,076
A pulmonary sarcoma?

328
00:19:06,545 --> 00:19:08,180
A malignant tumour with
a poor prognosis...

329
00:19:08,247 --> 00:19:10,249
is formed in the pulmonary artery.

330
00:19:10,549 --> 00:19:11,683
It's not an embolism?

331
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:14,820
This is a very rare tumour.

332
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:19,024
When shown on images such as
chest X-rays and CT's,

333
00:19:19,591 --> 00:19:22,594
it can look very similar
to an embolism,

334
00:19:22,661 --> 00:19:24,663
leading doctors to a wrong
diagnosis quite common.

335
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:29,601
However, a complete ablation of a tumour
of this sort, is very difficult.

336
00:19:30,369 --> 00:19:31,837
It's best not to operate.

337
00:19:35,874 --> 00:19:37,242
That's why I will do it.

338
00:19:46,385 --> 00:19:48,220
A pulmonary sarcoma?

339
00:19:48,887 --> 00:19:50,822
I'm sorry I failed to notice it.

340
00:19:50,956 --> 00:19:51,857
I'm very sorry.

341
00:19:51,924 --> 00:19:54,359
Failing to notice it?

342
00:19:54,426 --> 00:19:57,229
A tumour and embolism are
two very different things!

343
00:19:57,763 --> 00:19:59,965
Without treatment, she will
die within one month.

344
00:20:00,032 --> 00:20:01,800
What a terrible situation.

345
00:20:02,167 --> 00:20:03,802
Kaji. Chief-substitute.

346
00:20:04,303 --> 00:20:06,405
- Yes?
- Will you be able to operate on her?

347
00:20:06,772 --> 00:20:07,773
Well...

348
00:20:07,839 --> 00:20:08,674
I will do it.

349
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:12,211
Demon, this surgery isn't easy,
even for you.

350
00:20:12,277 --> 00:20:13,845
Don't worry. I never...

351
00:20:13,912 --> 00:20:16,248
It's not about failing or not!

352
00:20:16,782 --> 00:20:21,720
Do you really think I would
approve such risky surgery?

353
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:23,055
- Yes, sir.
- Why not?

354
00:20:23,121 --> 00:20:24,323
Why?

355
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:30,028
Because the patient
is from Keirin Hospital.

356
00:20:30,095 --> 00:20:32,397
If it doesn't go well,

357
00:20:32,564 --> 00:20:35,267
and she loses her life,
our hospital ranking will go down,

358
00:20:35,334 --> 00:20:36,902
which is really problematic.

359
00:20:36,969 --> 00:20:38,670
So are you...

360
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:40,272
We've been set up.

361
00:20:40,872 --> 00:20:41,840
Set up?

362
00:20:42,641 --> 00:20:45,510
My guess is that Keirin hospital
already knew this.

363
00:20:45,677 --> 00:20:47,746
They've gone through
examinations already...

364
00:20:48,247 --> 00:20:51,316
and realised it'd be very risky,
giving up on the surgery.

365
00:20:51,383 --> 00:20:53,118
They know she'll die.

366
00:20:53,652 --> 00:20:58,156
And they want her to die
particularly at Toutei Hospital.

367
00:20:58,390 --> 00:21:02,961
Keirin sent her here to lower our ranking.

368
00:21:03,095 --> 00:21:06,932
That Samejima is a cunning man.

369
00:21:06,999 --> 00:21:08,734
What a dreadful man.

370
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:10,002
This is terrible.

371
00:21:10,736 --> 00:21:15,240
But I already accepted his gift.

372
00:21:15,307 --> 00:21:16,275
You already did.

373
00:21:16,341 --> 00:21:18,143
- Excuse me.
- What?

374
00:21:18,477 --> 00:21:20,012
If you have time to talk about
such trivial things,

375
00:21:20,078 --> 00:21:21,146
let me operate already.

376
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,481
Like I said,

377
00:21:22,714 --> 00:21:26,285
I will not permit you to
perform such a risky surgery.

378
00:21:26,351 --> 00:21:29,154
- Don't you know why she came here?
- Huh?

379
00:21:29,655 --> 00:21:31,290
Of course,
it's because she wants to live!

380
00:21:32,391 --> 00:21:33,225
I will do the operation.

381
00:21:34,526 --> 00:21:35,360
Daimon,

382
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:37,629
wait.

383
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:40,632
It's become nettlesome now.

384
00:21:40,966 --> 00:21:44,736
The patient persistently
wants to get treatment here.

385
00:21:44,936 --> 00:21:46,038
If we refuse,

386
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:51,843
a rumour that we drove out a patient
from a rival hospital will spread.

387
00:21:53,512 --> 00:21:55,414
If you aren't able to
make a decision,

388
00:21:55,881 --> 00:21:58,850
why don't you ask
your beautiful wife?

389
00:21:59,251 --> 00:22:01,953
You have a beautiful wife, Hiruma.

390
00:22:05,357 --> 00:22:09,194
You knew, didn't you?
You knew about your disease.

391
00:22:14,199 --> 00:22:16,568
I can't get the operation
with high failure chance...

392
00:22:17,202 --> 00:22:19,571
at Keirin hospital.

393
00:22:20,906 --> 00:22:23,208
That's why you don't want
your husband to operate.

394
00:22:27,612 --> 00:22:32,284
He told me to let him do it.

395
00:22:32,551 --> 00:22:37,756
I also would want my husband
to save me if there was a chance.

396
00:22:38,323 --> 00:22:39,157
However,

397
00:22:40,959 --> 00:22:41,793
I can't.

398
00:22:42,527 --> 00:22:44,396
He's about to be promoted.

399
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,035
I cannot leave a blemish on his career.

400
00:22:52,003 --> 00:22:52,871
More than anything,

401
00:22:54,106 --> 00:22:56,274
if he is unable to save me,

402
00:22:57,342 --> 00:23:00,212
he will have to live with a sense
of guilt for the rest of his life.

403
00:23:02,247 --> 00:23:06,118
I could never do something like that.

404
00:23:10,489 --> 00:23:12,190
When I came across you,

405
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:15,794
I thought that by any chance,
you may be able to help me.

406
00:23:16,995 --> 00:23:17,829
But...

407
00:23:21,767 --> 00:23:23,301
I guess I was wrong.

408
00:23:28,039 --> 00:23:29,040
You're not.

409
00:23:35,447 --> 00:23:36,381
Let me operate.

410
00:23:39,351 --> 00:23:41,953
I never fail.

411
00:23:59,571 --> 00:24:00,605
Thank you.

412
00:24:06,745 --> 00:24:07,579
Everyone.

413
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:11,149
Toutei hospital is faced
with a crisis.

414
00:24:11,616 --> 00:24:14,886
Let's use our strength
to help them.

415
00:24:15,353 --> 00:24:16,288
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

416
00:24:23,862 --> 00:24:26,798
Popular Hospitals Website.

417
00:24:27,299 --> 00:24:28,567
I wrote it.

418
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:30,469
The wife of a doctor at Keirin

419
00:24:30,602 --> 00:24:33,371
is pushing for treatment...

420
00:24:33,438 --> 00:24:35,574
of her serious illness,
at another hospital.

421
00:24:36,174 --> 00:24:40,111
Okay. I left a review
on another website.

422
00:24:40,378 --> 00:24:41,746
A terrible hospital that

423
00:24:42,180 --> 00:24:44,883
lets its family member die.

424
00:24:45,317 --> 00:24:50,288
I also wrote a review
on a university hospital news platform.

425
00:24:50,355 --> 00:24:52,891
I submitted one on a
hidden hospital incidents board.

426
00:24:52,958 --> 00:24:55,327
I wrote on "Hospitals
you should never go to" page.

427
00:24:55,393 --> 00:24:57,596
Thank you very much, everyone.

428
00:25:00,732 --> 00:25:03,735
This will make them act right away.

429
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:05,070
- Yes ma'am.
- Yes ma'am.

430
00:25:12,844 --> 00:25:15,113
Let's start the discharge
paperwork immediately.

431
00:25:15,981 --> 00:25:18,450
There are rumours going around about you.

432
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:20,986
Director Hiruma humiliated
my husband...

433
00:25:21,052 --> 00:25:24,389
at an academic meeting.

434
00:25:25,123 --> 00:25:26,157
This is so shameful.

435
00:25:27,659 --> 00:25:30,996
The surgery will be
performed at our hospital.

436
00:25:31,963 --> 00:25:34,099
The surgeon in charge
will be your husband.

437
00:25:34,533 --> 00:25:38,737
Ma'am, I plan to
have my surgery here...

438
00:25:42,807 --> 00:25:43,775
Ms. Emi,

439
00:25:44,476 --> 00:25:48,914
your husband will become
a professor soon...

440
00:25:49,781 --> 00:25:53,318
if he succeeds in your surgery.

441
00:26:00,091 --> 00:26:01,793
Get out lumps!

442
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:04,930
- Go away lumps!
- It feels so good.

443
00:26:09,267 --> 00:26:11,636
Hey, hey. You scared me.

444
00:26:12,337 --> 00:26:13,572
My heart almost stopped.

445
00:26:14,439 --> 00:26:15,840
Knock first.

446
00:26:15,907 --> 00:26:18,243
Why is the patient
returning to Keirin?

447
00:26:19,144 --> 00:26:21,046
Huh? What are you talking about?

448
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:24,849
If I don't operate, she will die.

449
00:26:24,916 --> 00:26:27,419
She requested it, so there is nothing

450
00:26:27,485 --> 00:26:28,920
we can do about it.

451
00:26:29,020 --> 00:26:31,590
She is a member of
the women's association.

452
00:26:32,023 --> 00:26:33,558
Her pride is more important
than her life.

453
00:26:33,625 --> 00:26:35,360
Life is more important!

454
00:26:36,661 --> 00:26:38,296
Don't yell!

455
00:26:38,363 --> 00:26:39,764
Are you dumb?

456
00:26:42,767 --> 00:26:43,602
Hey,

457
00:26:44,502 --> 00:26:45,570
Daimon.

458
00:26:45,637 --> 00:26:50,542
How dare you call Director of
Toutei University Hospital dumb?

459
00:26:52,677 --> 00:26:53,645
Hey, Michiko Daimon.

460
00:26:54,479 --> 00:26:56,514
You are nothing more
than a part-timer.

461
00:26:57,716 --> 00:26:58,683
Get out.

462
00:27:01,119 --> 00:27:02,053
Get out.

463
00:27:05,657 --> 00:27:06,825
Leave.

464
00:27:31,416 --> 00:27:35,720
Daimon, how long are you going to
have that sour look on your face?

465
00:27:35,854 --> 00:27:38,757
- Yeah, let's have a good time!
- Don't be depressed.

466
00:27:38,890 --> 00:27:40,592
Why are you even here?

467
00:27:42,594 --> 00:27:45,063
I heard that you're depressed,

468
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:47,932
so we came to console you.
Oh, I win.

469
00:27:48,333 --> 00:27:50,835
You just came to kill some time
after drinking, didn't you?

470
00:27:50,902 --> 00:27:55,640
It's because both of them
can't just let her leave untreated.

471
00:27:55,707 --> 00:27:56,841
That's right.

472
00:27:56,941 --> 00:28:01,012
There you go again,
you're rubbing salt in one's wounds.

473
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:03,248
You're so loud.

474
00:28:04,549 --> 00:28:05,817
You're just fake crying.

475
00:28:08,253 --> 00:28:10,722
I hope they succeed
in her surgery at least.

476
00:28:10,889 --> 00:28:13,625
We can't do anything
about it anymore.

477
00:28:13,758 --> 00:28:17,629
Daimon, it's just like, you know.
That's how University Hospitals work.

478
00:28:17,696 --> 00:28:20,031
We have no choice.

479
00:28:20,231 --> 00:28:23,835
We, doctors, are no different
from those with other jobs.

480
00:28:23,902 --> 00:28:27,138
We have to endure
the burden of obligation.

481
00:28:27,372 --> 00:28:28,506
We are not people

482
00:28:28,573 --> 00:28:33,878
who can just live by our own
rules like you, Daimon!

483
00:28:38,283 --> 00:28:41,453
Daimon! It's your turn!

484
00:28:41,519 --> 00:28:42,821
What is it, Dr. Daimon?

485
00:28:46,991 --> 00:28:47,992
Kin, nice job.

486
00:28:48,226 --> 00:28:50,061
Nice? What is?

487
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:52,263
I win!

488
00:28:56,501 --> 00:28:58,536
- A super special combination!
- A super special combination!

489
00:28:59,270 --> 00:29:01,506
It's so rare for you to win, Michiko!

490
00:29:09,414 --> 00:29:10,348
SINGLE ROOM

491
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:11,783
Excuse me.

492
00:29:13,218 --> 00:29:14,185
Ms. Kujyo?

493
00:29:17,288 --> 00:29:18,156
Ms. Kujyo!

494
00:29:20,291 --> 00:29:21,893
Which part of your body is painful?

495
00:29:22,527 --> 00:29:23,361
Contact...

496
00:29:23,795 --> 00:29:24,662
Contact?

497
00:29:25,063 --> 00:29:25,930
Contact!

498
00:29:26,898 --> 00:29:28,767
Ms. Kujyo. Hang in there!

499
00:29:28,833 --> 00:29:29,901
Stretcher coming through!

500
00:29:29,968 --> 00:29:31,369
Please watch out!

501
00:29:31,503 --> 00:29:33,271
Breathe slowly.

502
00:29:33,338 --> 00:29:34,672
Excuse me.
Stretcher is coming through!

503
00:29:43,982 --> 00:29:48,319
The hospital director will now make
his rounds around the hospital.

504
00:29:48,386 --> 00:29:50,855
Good morning. Good day.

505
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:53,324
What a lovely morning.

506
00:29:53,825 --> 00:29:57,896
I want each one of you to do
your best to save more lives.

507
00:29:58,096 --> 00:29:59,531
Yes sir!

508
00:30:08,173 --> 00:30:09,674
Gosh.

509
00:30:09,941 --> 00:30:11,142
What should we do, sir?

510
00:30:14,579 --> 00:30:16,581
Michiko Daimon is here.

511
00:30:16,681 --> 00:30:18,616
- Huh?
- See. Look.

512
00:30:22,053 --> 00:30:23,288
Are you okay?

513
00:30:23,855 --> 00:30:25,456
She doesn't look anything like her!

514
00:30:30,094 --> 00:30:32,964
We will now begin the resection...

515
00:30:33,798 --> 00:30:35,934
of Emi Kujyo's pulmonary tumour.

516
00:30:37,302 --> 00:30:38,169
Let's do our best.

517
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:40,305
- Let's do our best.
- Let's do our best.

518
00:30:40,538 --> 00:30:41,706
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

519
00:31:00,758 --> 00:31:02,093
- Monopolar endoscope.
- Here you are.

520
00:31:09,801 --> 00:31:12,804
This operation is too hard
for Dr. Kujyo.

521
00:31:15,039 --> 00:31:16,808
Still, it will become a sad story...

522
00:31:19,043 --> 00:31:21,679
of a surgeon
who tried to save his wife.

523
00:31:23,081 --> 00:31:24,582
The result doesn't really matter.

524
00:31:25,483 --> 00:31:26,317
- Yes sir.
- Yes sir.

525
00:31:40,265 --> 00:31:42,533
- I'm sorry, Wipe my sweat.
- Excuse me.

526
00:31:50,441 --> 00:31:51,542
I can't see anything.

527
00:31:53,511 --> 00:31:55,079
I cannot see the location
of the tumour.

528
00:31:56,781 --> 00:31:59,083
- Let's open further.
- Yes, sir.

529
00:31:59,417 --> 00:32:00,718
- Scalpel again.
- Here you are.

530
00:32:06,324 --> 00:32:07,225
What is this?

531
00:32:07,992 --> 00:32:12,397
The tumour is completely
blocking the passage.

532
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:14,766
It has moved inside the atrium.

533
00:32:18,903 --> 00:32:21,139
I will separate the tumour.

534
00:32:21,839 --> 00:32:22,740
- Separator.
- Here you are.

535
00:32:26,277 --> 00:32:27,378
Shoot.

536
00:32:41,092 --> 00:32:43,261
It's too strongly adhered
to the blood vessel.

537
00:32:47,932 --> 00:32:50,935
He can't remove it after all.

538
00:32:53,237 --> 00:32:55,006
So that's how it is.

539
00:32:57,342 --> 00:32:58,276
Mark it as inoperable.

540
00:32:59,043 --> 00:33:00,044
Yes sir.

541
00:33:06,918 --> 00:33:07,752
Emi.

542
00:33:10,288 --> 00:33:11,289
I'm so sorry.

543
00:33:23,968 --> 00:33:24,936
Who is that?

544
00:33:29,207 --> 00:33:30,241
Dr. Daimon!

545
00:33:32,176 --> 00:33:33,077
Okay, take a spell.

546
00:33:34,746 --> 00:33:35,713
What are you doing?

547
00:33:35,913 --> 00:33:37,348
I'm checking.

548
00:33:37,482 --> 00:33:39,951
That's not what I mean.
Why are you here?

549
00:33:40,985 --> 00:33:43,421
Hey! Who are you?

550
00:33:43,554 --> 00:33:45,323
You can't break
in the operation room.

551
00:33:47,492 --> 00:33:48,659
Excuse me.

552
00:33:50,294 --> 00:33:52,730
I am from Kanbara
excellent physician referral centre.

553
00:33:53,064 --> 00:33:54,732
Excellent physician referral centre?

554
00:33:54,799 --> 00:33:57,869
After receiving a call
that there would be...

555
00:33:57,935 --> 00:33:59,971
an emergency operation,
we rushed here.

556
00:34:00,438 --> 00:34:02,507
I'm relieved we made it in time.

557
00:34:02,673 --> 00:34:04,342
What are you talking about?

558
00:34:04,409 --> 00:34:10,081
We have a personal contract
with your patient, Emi Kujyo.

559
00:34:10,281 --> 00:34:11,816
It's written that

560
00:34:11,949 --> 00:34:16,621
our doctor, Michiko Daimon, shall
assist Dr. Kujyo during the operation.

561
00:34:16,687 --> 00:34:17,955
AKIRA KANBARA AND EMI KUJYO

562
00:34:18,256 --> 00:34:21,125
The patient has the right
to choose the surgeon.

563
00:34:21,192 --> 00:34:26,264
I don't think you can kick out
Dr. Daimon now.

564
00:34:26,330 --> 00:34:28,633
Will we get any merits
through this?

565
00:34:28,900 --> 00:34:30,268
I'm afraid to tell you that...

566
00:34:30,435 --> 00:34:31,769
Dr. Daimon cares

567
00:34:32,136 --> 00:34:36,174
only about her patients unlike you.

568
00:34:37,008 --> 00:34:40,344
Let me make it clear that we're
not responsible for any mistakes

569
00:34:42,847 --> 00:34:43,981
that occur during the surgery.

570
00:34:44,549 --> 00:34:45,917
I am well aware of that.

571
00:34:46,350 --> 00:34:49,687
However, there's no need to worry.

572
00:34:50,221 --> 00:34:51,189
That is because...

573
00:34:56,694 --> 00:34:58,196
I never fail.

574
00:35:03,468 --> 00:35:06,170
Michiko, perform
with all your might.

575
00:35:08,906 --> 00:35:10,875
Stop staring off and help me.

576
00:35:11,175 --> 00:35:12,477
No, I...

577
00:35:12,610 --> 00:35:13,945
You're a surgeon too, right?

578
00:35:15,446 --> 00:35:18,149
Don't worry.
I won't let you fail, either.

579
00:35:18,983 --> 00:35:20,651
Let's continue to
cut out the tumour.

580
00:35:20,751 --> 00:35:22,186
- Lower my magnifier.
- Excuse me.

581
00:35:23,421 --> 00:35:24,589
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

582
00:35:50,615 --> 00:35:55,653
It is impossible to completely
remove that tumour.

583
00:35:56,787 --> 00:35:59,891
Even here at Keirin,
Japan's top hospital,

584
00:36:00,024 --> 00:36:01,392
no one can do it.

585
00:36:01,926 --> 00:36:02,760
Yes sir.

586
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:04,095
I'm sorry,

587
00:36:04,662 --> 00:36:11,068
but Dr. Daimon isn't just the best.
She's the best of best.

588
00:36:26,117 --> 00:36:27,151
Starting removal.

589
00:36:27,218 --> 00:36:28,286
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

590
00:36:41,999 --> 00:36:43,067
Incredible.

591
00:36:43,634 --> 00:36:44,802
Don't just stare.

592
00:36:46,003 --> 00:36:47,638
Pull on the stump of the tumour.

593
00:36:47,772 --> 00:36:49,073
Okay.

594
00:37:02,453 --> 00:37:03,287
She's so fast.

595
00:37:05,289 --> 00:37:07,992
She removes that firmly
adhered tumour.

596
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,501
Tumour is removed.

597
00:37:17,568 --> 00:37:20,137
Next, I will rebuild the
right ventricular outflow tract.

598
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:22,840
Dr. Daimon, how about
a complete removal of the left side?

599
00:37:22,907 --> 00:37:24,175
I refuse.

600
00:37:24,342 --> 00:37:26,811
What if the tumour grows again?

601
00:37:26,911 --> 00:37:28,579
If the tumour is removed completely,

602
00:37:28,646 --> 00:37:30,848
there is no risk of
the tumour spreading further.

603
00:37:31,616 --> 00:37:33,384
Let's hurry the next procedure.

604
00:37:33,451 --> 00:37:34,518
- Scalpel.
- Here you are.

605
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:39,190
First assistant, begin
simultaneously stitching the lungs.

606
00:37:39,724 --> 00:37:42,260
Got it. Continuous suture.

607
00:37:42,326 --> 00:37:43,861
- 60 polypropylene.
- Yes, sir.

608
00:37:44,629 --> 00:37:45,463
So you knew this.

609
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:47,098
Yes.

610
00:38:06,183 --> 00:38:08,419
We're done.
What was the blood loss?

611
00:38:08,486 --> 00:38:09,654
100 cc.

612
00:38:10,588 --> 00:38:13,124
- Good work.
- Good work.

613
00:38:18,929 --> 00:38:21,565
Your husband isn't
as bad as you think.

614
00:38:26,537 --> 00:38:27,638
Thank you!

615
00:38:35,780 --> 00:38:38,616
Director, it was a success!

616
00:38:39,583 --> 00:38:43,387
The scenario of the husband saving
his wife has come true perfectly!

617
00:38:48,326 --> 00:38:51,262
If it had turned out bad, you
wouldn't have taken responsibility.

618
00:38:51,462 --> 00:38:54,398
However, do you take credit
for the success now?

619
00:38:55,099 --> 00:38:57,501
That is shameless.

620
00:38:59,270 --> 00:39:02,640
However, depending on
the circumstances...

621
00:39:02,773 --> 00:39:06,210
we might let you take the credit.

622
00:39:10,614 --> 00:39:11,449
How much?

623
00:39:12,717 --> 00:39:15,019
I assumed this would happen, so...

624
00:39:18,389 --> 00:39:19,623
Here is a melon.

625
00:39:19,990 --> 00:39:20,825
Melon?

626
00:39:22,193 --> 00:39:23,894
Here is the bill.

627
00:39:24,362 --> 00:39:25,229
Here you are.

628
00:39:26,464 --> 00:39:27,331
Here you are.

629
00:39:33,671 --> 00:39:34,572
10 million dollars?

630
00:39:34,972 --> 00:39:37,708
What is this ridiculous amount?

631
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,643
Congratulations.

632
00:39:40,277 --> 00:39:46,417
With this, Keirin will be able
to maintain the top place.

633
00:39:55,526 --> 00:40:00,631
Michiko! It was a huge success!

634
00:40:01,298 --> 00:40:02,566
Mr. Akira! I'm so hungry!

635
00:40:02,633 --> 00:40:05,236
I will treat you to whatever
you would like today.

636
00:40:05,302 --> 00:40:06,303
Really?

637
00:40:06,437 --> 00:40:08,506
The cafeteria here is so famous.

638
00:40:08,973 --> 00:40:10,608
No way. I want barbecue.

639
00:40:10,841 --> 00:40:12,843
I got it. Let's have meat, Mitsuko.

640
00:40:13,811 --> 00:40:16,647
Special spare rib!

641
00:40:20,751 --> 00:40:22,887
Special spare rib!

642
00:40:23,154 --> 00:40:25,389
The surgery was a success?

643
00:40:25,523 --> 00:40:28,893
Emi Kujyo is said to be
making a full recovery.

644
00:40:32,530 --> 00:40:34,098
After the succeed in surgery,

645
00:40:34,165 --> 00:40:36,500
Keirin's ratings are
going through the roof.

646
00:40:37,735 --> 00:40:38,903
She removed that tumour?

647
00:40:40,337 --> 00:40:41,172
No way.

648
00:40:41,305 --> 00:40:43,841
I heard from an acquaintance
that there was...

649
00:40:44,241 --> 00:40:47,278
a superior surgeon who preformed
the surgery with Dr. Kujyo.

650
00:40:48,112 --> 00:40:49,313
It was a woman.

651
00:40:50,047 --> 00:40:51,182
A woman?

652
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:54,919
She was said to be
a skilful yet rude,

653
00:40:55,553 --> 00:40:58,622
reckless yet strong,
woman physician.

654
00:40:58,689 --> 00:41:01,659
Kikawada.
Don't say anything dumb.

655
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:06,397
There are many women
who fit exactly that description!

656
00:41:09,767 --> 00:41:11,502
I'm just a part-timer.

657
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:29,587
It must be nice to
have so much freedom.

658
00:41:29,653 --> 00:41:30,488
Freedom.

659
00:41:48,739 --> 00:41:51,342
I'm glad we were able to make it
in time to the dance contest.

660
00:42:05,956 --> 00:42:10,628
In the end,
Toutei is nothing compared to us...

661
00:42:10,961 --> 00:42:13,264
even in this dance contest.

662
00:42:13,464 --> 00:42:14,632
- Yes ma'am.
- Yes ma'am.

663
00:42:19,503 --> 00:42:21,639
Keirin is superior after all.

664
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:27,745
Even so, why does Director Hiruma's wife
have such a smug look on her face?

665
00:42:28,479 --> 00:42:29,313
She does.

666
00:42:34,418 --> 00:42:37,054
What? They changed music.

667
00:42:48,198 --> 00:42:51,135
- Look.
- Gosh.

668
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:02,713
Who is that woman?

669
00:43:02,780 --> 00:43:05,549
I don't know what's on her mind,

670
00:43:06,517 --> 00:43:10,154
but it was definitely a good decision
to have her here as support.

671
00:43:10,554 --> 00:43:11,388
- Yes ma'am.
- Yes ma'am.

672
00:43:23,033 --> 00:43:24,868
She's the chief of public
relations department

673
00:43:24,935 --> 00:43:26,837
and she even has connections
with the financial sector.

674
00:43:27,004 --> 00:43:27,972
She is great.

675
00:43:28,038 --> 00:43:30,040
Yes. She is great.

676
00:43:40,384 --> 00:43:43,721
The champion is
Toutei women's association.

677
00:43:46,523 --> 00:43:47,691
Congratulations!

678
00:43:48,425 --> 00:43:51,528
It's so heavy!

679
00:43:53,330 --> 00:43:56,100
It's so heavy!

680
00:43:59,837 --> 00:44:02,940
- It's okay, you tried your best.
- It's heavy!

681
00:44:13,584 --> 00:44:16,754
<i>This is the story of a lone wolf,</i>
<i>female physician.</i>

682
00:44:27,264 --> 00:44:28,999
You're a good dancer.

683
00:44:32,236 --> 00:44:33,404
Thank you.

684
00:44:40,010 --> 00:44:41,111
What?

685
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:47,718
What was that?

686
00:44:48,786 --> 00:44:51,522
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>

687
00:44:52,089 --> 00:44:53,190
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

688
00:44:54,258 --> 00:44:57,194
<i>Her solo weapons are her license and...</i>

689
00:44:57,761 --> 00:44:59,129
<i>the skills she has earned.</i>

690
00:45:03,934 --> 00:45:06,036
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

691
00:45:06,670 --> 00:45:07,604
<i>Also known as</i>

692
00:45:08,205 --> 00:45:09,640
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

693
00:45:10,974 --> 00:45:12,209
Shall we?

694
00:45:14,011 --> 00:45:15,312
THE LAST EPISODE

695
00:45:15,379 --> 00:45:17,748
So you don't care
what happens to your wife.

696
00:45:17,815 --> 00:45:20,184
Women are not
child-bearing machines!

697
00:45:20,250 --> 00:45:22,352
A simultaneous mother and
unborn child surgery?

698
00:45:22,419 --> 00:45:23,887
There is a uterus haemorrhage.

699
00:45:23,954 --> 00:45:26,056
There are things one cannot
do anything about.

700
00:45:26,790 --> 00:45:28,859
Don't attend the operations.
